<title>FRANCE: French shares resume advance after lower Wall St.</title>
<headline>French shares resume advance after lower Wall St.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares resumed their rise on Tuesday afternoon despite a lower start on Wall Street as U.S. investors did not ply in to sell French stocks.</p>
<p>Market in rebound from Monday's 3.9 percent fall.</p>
<p>President Jacques Chirac due to make televised address at 1800 GMT.</p>
<p>* CAC-40 index up 19.35 points, or 0.73 percent, at 2,674.09</p>
<p>* CAC-40 May futures 2,670 vs 2,656 at Monday's close</p>
<p>* Of CAC-40 stocks, 26 higher, 14 lower</p>
<p>* Broader SBF-120 index up 12.68 at 1,840.34</p>
<p>* Total volume 5.5 billion francs</p>
</text>
